      "credit": "U.S. Navy photo by Mass Communication Specialist 2nd Class Roger S. Duncan",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "description": "Chemeril, Kenya – (Aug. 5, 2006) - A Pokot girl poses for a photograph during the Veterinary Civil Assistance Project (VETCAP) operated by U.S., Kenyan, Tanzanian and Ugandan veterinarians and doctors. Her neckpiece signifies that she is engaged to be married. During exercise Natural Fire, over 2000 sheep and goats were vaccinated against Sheep Pox and Pleural Pneumonia at a Veterinary Civil Assistance Project (VETCAP) operated by U.S., Kenyan, Tanzanian and Ugandan veterinarians and doctors. Natural Fire is the largest combined exercise between Eastern African community nations and the United States, and includes medical, veterinary and engineering civic affairs programs. U.S. Navy photo by Mass Communication Specialist 2nd Class Roger S. Duncan (RELEASED)",
